<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Physician writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-562"}>{"Papers "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-563"}>{"Support "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Send the case "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-562"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"}>{"Case report"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"}>{"Original research article"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"}>{"Physician manuscripts"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"}>{"Clinical literature review"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-563"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"}>{"Research proposal"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"}>{"Literature search & citation"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/customized-writing/"}>{"Customized writing"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-training/"}>{"Physician training"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Clinical Literature Review Service"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1 className={"h1--long "}>{"Clinical Literature Review for Evidence-Based Medicine"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"“Literature review” covers six different products that cost between a fortnight and six months, and choosing wrongly is the most expensive mistake in evidence synthesis. A scoping review cannot answer an effect question. A systematic review cannot be done properly in three weeks by one person, whatever the proposal says. A regulatory literature review for a clinical evaluation report is judged against a submission template rather than against PRISMA. Pubrica’s clinical literature review service starts by settling which review your question and your timeline actually support, then runs it properly — protocol first, search documented so anybody can repeat it, appraisal with the instrument that fits the studies rather than the one everybody cites, and certainty graded per outcome."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#cl-chooser"}>{"Find out which review you need"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-cl"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cl"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"One review at a glance"}</b>{" · an effect question"}</span> <span>{"PRISMA 2020 · 5 databases"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Protocol registered before screening began"}</b><span>{"PROSPERO"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Search strategy reported in full, per database"}</b><span>{"PRISMA-S"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Screened independently by two reviewers"}</b><span>{"Dual"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Risk of bias judged per outcome, not per study"}</b><span>{"RoB 2"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Certainty graded, with the reasons given"}</b><span>{"GRADE"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Question"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" protocol "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" search "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" screen "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" appraise "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"synthesis"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every review"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Protocol before search"}</li> <li>{"Search reported in full"}</li> <li>{"Appraised by domain"}</li> <li>{"Certainty graded"}</li> <li>{"Repeatable by a stranger"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $340"}</b><span>{"A narrative or targeted review, in 7–10 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Evidence synthesis for clinicians, industry and HTA teams"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"PRISMA 2020 · GRADE"}</b><span>{"With PRISMA-S for the search and PRISMA-ScR for scoping reviews"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-what-we-do-6oxxkk"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-who-we-serve-1gfgqc2"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-our-complianc-15bk7yn"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-how-it-works-t9xtlc"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-our-experts-klbwt1"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-sample-work-94a80x"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-packages-1ej4o5c"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-guarantee-15wg7th"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-client-storie-g3ntw"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-literature-review-faq-1jfquw3"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-what-we-do-6oxxkk"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Nine pieces of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Reviews arrive at every stage. Some are a question and a deadline; some are four thousand screened records and a team that has run out of evenings. Any stage can be picked up."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Question framing and review scoping"}</b> <span>{"The question framed in PICO, SPIDER or PIRD so that it can actually be searched, and the review type chosen from what the question and the timeline support. Sold as a standalone scoping conversation with a written recommendation, and credited against the review if you commission one. This is the hour that most often changes the shape and the cost."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Protocol development and registration"}</b> <span>{"A protocol written to PRISMA-P and registered on PROSPERO, or on the Open Science Framework for a scoping review. Inclusion criteria, outcome hierarchy, analysis plan, appraisal instrument and disagreement procedure, all fixed before the search runs. Registration is handled and the record kept updated as the review proceeds."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Search strategy design and execution"}</b> <span>{"Built by somebody who builds searches, tested against known items before it is run, translated correctly between database syntaxes rather than pasted between them, and saved with every date, interface and result count. MEDLINE, Embase, the Cochrane Library, Scopus, Web of Science, CINAHL, PsycINFO, trial registries and grey literature as the question requires."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Screening and selection"}</b> <span>{"Two reviewers independently at title and abstract and again at full text, with disagreement resolved by discussion and a third reader where it persists, agreement measured, and every full-text exclusion recorded with its reason. Delivered with the PRISMA flow diagram populated from the actual counts rather than reconstructed afterwards."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Data extraction"}</b> <span>{"Into a form piloted on a handful of studies before it is used on all of them, with outcome data extracted in duplicate. Authors contacted where data is missing or reported only in a figure, and the outcome of that contact recorded — which is a reportable item and an informative one. The extraction file is delivered to you, not just its summary."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Risk of bias and quality appraisal"}</b> <span>{"With the instrument that fits the studies: RoB 2 for randomised trials judged per outcome, ROBINS-I for non-randomised interventions with the version stated, ROBINS-E for exposures, QUADAS-3 for diagnostic accuracy, AMSTAR 2 for reviews, CASP for qualitative work. Domain judgements reported, not a summary score."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Synthesis and meta-analysis"}</b> <span>{"Narrative synthesis where the studies will not combine, meta-analysis where they will, and an explicit decision either way rather than a default. Heterogeneity quantified, explored by subgroup and meta-regression where there is enough data, and explained. Sensitivity analyses that test the conclusion rather than decorate it. Forest and funnel plots built to journal specification."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"GRADE and the summary of findings"}</b> <span>{"Certainty rated per outcome with every downgrade justified in a sentence a reader can check, and a summary-of-findings table a clinician can use without reading the review around it. GRADE-CERQual where the evidence is qualitative. This is the part guideline panels and HTA reviewers read first and the part most often left thin."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Regulatory and HTA literature review"}</b> <span>{"Targeted literature reviews written into a submission rather than into a journal: the clinical evaluation literature appendix for an EU MDR technical file, the evidence section of an HTA or payer dossier, the background for an IND, NDA, BLA or 510(k). Version-controlled as a document inside a file, with the search auditable and re-runnable to a stated date."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-who-we-serve-1gfgqc2"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Two audiences, and we do not pretend they are one."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A regulatory affairs team assembling a clinical evaluation and a specialty trainee writing a first review need the same rigour and completely different products. These are commonly sold from one set of packages, which serves neither."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Clinicians and guideline developers"}</b><span>{"A question from practice that needs an answer the department can act on, graded so that the strength of the recommendation is visible. Usually a systematic or rapid review, and usually with a real deadline attached to a meeting."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Academic researchers and postgraduates"}</b><span>{"A review for publication or for a thesis, where the review is itself the research output and has to survive peer review on its method rather than its conclusion. Registration and dual screening are not optional here."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Medical device manufacturers and notified-body submissions"}</b><span>{"The literature appendix of a clinical evaluation report under the EU MDR or IVDR, where the search has to be auditable, re-runnable and version-controlled, and where the reviewer is an auditor rather than a journal editor."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Pharmaceutical and biotech teams"}</b><span>{"Background evidence for an IND, NDA, BLA or 510(k), pipeline landscaping, and comparative effectiveness work. Where the study is company-sponsored, GPP 2022 applies alongside the ICMJE and the sponsor’s role is disclosed."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"HTA, payer and market access teams"}</b><span>{"Targeted literature reviews written into a submission template, with the evidence base characterised honestly — including where it is thin, because an assessor who finds the gap you did not mention reads everything else differently."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Hospitals, CROs and research units"}</b><span>{"Standing review capacity for departments producing several a year, where the constraint is throughput and consistency rather than any single question, and a house method settled once is worth more than any individual review."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Where the evidence turns out to be thin"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"It happens often, and it is the moment that separates a review from a marketing document. A search returns four studies, three of them small and one at high risk of bias, and the honest synthesis says the evidence is insufficient to answer the question. Nobody commissions a review hoping for that. But an HTA assessor, a notified body reviewer or a guideline panel will find the same four studies in an afternoon, and a review that characterised the base optimistically is then worth less than no review at all — because it tells the assessor something about the submitter rather than about the evidence. We report what is there. Where it is thin we say so, quantify how thin, and set out what would have to be done to answer the question properly, which is frequently the most valuable output of the whole exercise."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-our-complianc-15bk7yn"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The instruments, and which version is current."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Appraisal instruments are revised, and using a superseded one is visible to any reviewer who works in the field. Two of the five below changed in the last two years, and one widely cited instrument has been retired from our list entirely."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"PRISMA 2020"}>{"PRISMA"}<em>{"2020 · + S, ScR"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"PRISMA 2020 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(reporting a systematic review)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The reporting guideline for systematic reviews, in its 2020 revision; there is no later version. PRISMA-S covers the search strategy and is what makes a search repeatable rather than merely described. PRISMA-ScR covers scoping reviews, which PRISMA 2020 itself does not. PRISMA is a reporting standard, not a conduct standard — it tells you what to write down, not how to do the review. The Cochrane Handbook is the conduct reference, and the two are complementary rather than alternatives."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"GRADE"}>{"GRADE"}<em>{"per outcome"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"GRADE "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(certainty of the evidence)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Certainty is rated per outcome, not per review, and the reason for every downgrade is stated: risk of bias, inconsistency, indirectness, imprecision, publication bias. A summary-of-findings table that gives one certainty rating for the whole review has misunderstood the instrument, and it is a common enough error that reviewers look for it. For qualitative evidence the equivalent is GRADE-CERQual, which assesses confidence in a finding rather than certainty of an effect."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"RoB 2 and ROBINS-I"}>{"RoB 2"}<em>{"ROBINS-I · QUADAS-3"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Risk of bias "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(the instrument follows the studies)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"RoB 2 for randomised trials, judged per outcome rather than per study. ROBINS-I for non-randomised studies of interventions — noting that ROBINS-I V2 has circulated as a draft and is not yet the settled version, so the version used should be stated. ROBINS-E for exposure studies. QUADAS-3 for diagnostic accuracy, which superseded QUADAS-2 in February 2026; a review submitted now using QUADAS-2 will be asked about it. AMSTAR 2 where the things being appraised are themselves systematic reviews."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"PROSPERO"}>{"PROSPERO"}<em>{"before screening"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Prospective registration "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(what the protocol is actually for)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"PROSPERO for systematic reviews, rapid reviews and umbrella reviews; the Open Science Framework for scoping reviews, which PROSPERO does not take. Registration before screening begins is what supports every claim the review makes about its own method, and the registration date is permanently visible. Deviations from the protocol are entirely acceptable and happen in most reviews — what is not acceptable is silent deviation, so each one is reported with its reason."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Two things you will find on other pages that are not on this one"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}><b>{"The Jadad scale."}</b>{" It still appears in the standards lists of a great many medical writing sites. Cochrane advises against summary quality scores of this type, and the reason is straightforward: collapsing several unrelated domains into one number hides which domain was the problem, and a trial can score three out of five while being at high risk of bias in the exact domain that matters for your outcome. Domain-based assessment replaced it more than a decade ago. "}<b>{"And the claim to work “to GPP3”."}</b>{" GPP3 dates from 2015 and was superseded by GPP 2022, published in the "}<i>{"Annals of Internal Medicine"}</i>{" and stewarded by ISMPP. It also only applies to company-sponsored research, so listing it on every page regardless of sponsorship is decoration rather than compliance. Where a review is company-sponsored, GPP 2022 applies and we say so."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Two people read every study that makes it in."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"What Pubrica holds to is which decisions a tool is allowed to make, rather than how much of the reading it can do. Every study that makes it in is read by two people, and the reader of your review is told where a tool was used."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Prioritisation, so the likely includes surface first. Deduplication. Flagging records whose reported outcome does not match the protocol."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Unsupervised include or exclude decisions; appraisal judgements; extraction accepted without a human check; and anything headed for a regulatory or HTA submission, where an assessor traces every judgement to a person."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-how-it-works-t9xtlc"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the clinical literature review service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the order is the method."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A systematic review is not a search followed by writing. It is a sequence in which each step is fixed before the next one can bias it, which is why running them out of order quietly destroys the claim."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"The question, framed so it can be answered"}</h3> <p><b>{"PICO for effect questions, SPIDER for qualitative ones, PIRD for diagnostic accuracy."}</b>{" This is also where the review type is settled — systematic, rapid, scoping, umbrella or regulatory — because that decision governs the cost, the timeline and what the review is allowed to conclude. A question that cannot be framed is usually a scoping review wearing the wrong label."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"Protocol, written and registered"}</h3> <p><b>{"To PRISMA-P, then registered on PROSPERO before any screening starts."}</b>{" Inclusion and exclusion criteria, the outcomes and their hierarchy, the planned analysis, the appraisal instrument and the handling of disagreement — all fixed while the results are still invisible. This is the stage that makes everything after it a systematic review rather than a literature search."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"The search, built once and reported in full"}</h3> <p><b>{"Controlled vocabulary and free text, per database, with the syntax that database actually uses."}</b>{" MEDLINE through PubMed or Ovid, Embase, the Cochrane Library, Scopus, Web of Science, plus trial registries and grey literature where the question needs them. Every strategy saved with its date, interface and result count and reported in an appendix to PRISMA-S, so somebody else can run it and get your numbers."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Screening, by two people independently"}</h3> <p><b>{"Title and abstract, then full text, with disagreement resolved by discussion and a third reviewer where it persists."}</b>{" Every full-text exclusion recorded with its reason, because that list is a reported item and reviewers read it. Agreement is measured rather than assumed. Where a rapid review uses single screening, that is stated in the methods rather than left to be inferred."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Extraction and appraisal"}</h3> <p><b>{"Into a piloted form, in duplicate for the outcome data."}</b>{" Risk of bias with the instrument that fits the studies rather than the one everybody cites, judged per outcome where the instrument works that way. Where data is missing we write to authors and record whether they replied — which is itself a reportable fact, and an unusually informative one."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Synthesis, and certainty"}</h3> <p><b>{"Narrative synthesis, meta-analysis or evidence mapping, chosen from what the studies will support rather than decided in advance."}</b>{" Heterogeneity quantified and explained rather than reported and passed over. GRADE applied per outcome with every downgrade justified, and a summary-of-findings table a clinician can read without the review around it."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the question. We will tell you which review it supports."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Two business days, at no cost: which review your question and your timeline actually support, how many weeks of work it is at that scale, and an honest word about whether the answer you are hoping for is one the literature can give. That last one saves more money than anything else we do."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The question"}</b><span>{"In a sentence, however rough"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The purpose"}</b><span>{"Paper, guideline, submission, dossier or grant"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The deadline"}</b><span>{"The real one, not the comfortable one"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The team"}</b><span>{"Who can screen, and who will be an author"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Any search"}</b><span>{"Strategies you have already run, and their counts"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Known studies"}</b><span>{"Three or four papers that must be in the results"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"Those three or four known studies are the most useful thing on the list. A search strategy that fails to retrieve papers you already know belong in the review is a broken strategy, and testing against known items is how that gets caught in the first hour rather than after four thousand records have been screened. If you have no known studies, say so — that is itself informative about the size of the field."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The decision that sets the cost"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Which review does your question actually support?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Almost every expensive problem in evidence synthesis starts here. Somebody commissions a systematic review for a question that is really a mapping exercise, or promises one in four weeks with a single reviewer, or writes a narrative review and gives it a flow diagram. Answer six questions and the chooser below names the review your question and your timeline support, the guideline that reports it, the instrument that appraises the studies you will actually find, and roughly how many weeks of work it is."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"cl-chooser"} data-tool={"rvt"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"cl-chooser-body"}>{"Review type chooser"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"Systematic, rapid, scoping, narrative, umbrella or regulatory — with the guideline, the registration route and the appraisal instrument that follow from each."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"cl-chooser-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-cl-use"}>{"What is the review for?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"use"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-cl-use"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"paper"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"A journal paper"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"clin"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A clinical or guideline decision"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"reg"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A regulatory submission"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"grant"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A grant or protocol"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"map"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Mapping a field"}</button></div></div> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-cl-scope"}>{"How tightly defined is the question?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"scope"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-cl-scope"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"tight"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"A specific population, intervention and outcome"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"broad"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Broad — what is out there on this topic"}</button></div></div> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-cl-pool"}>{"What kind of studies will you mostly find?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"pool"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-cl-pool"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"rct"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Randomised trials"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"nrsi"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Non-randomised interventions"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"obs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Observational or exposure studies"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"diag"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Diagnostic accuracy studies"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"qual"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Qualitative research"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"revs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Other systematic reviews"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Weeks available before you need it"}</span><input type={"number"} data-k={"weeks"} value={"12"} step={1} min={1} /></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"People who can screen and extract"}</span><em>{"Independent dual screening is what “systematic” rests on. One person is a rapid review, honestly labelled."}</em><input type={"number"} data-k={"revs"} value={"2"} step={1} min={1} /></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"comb"} /><span>{"The results need combining statistically"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"audit"} /><span>{"Somebody will audit or re-run the search — a regulator, a notified body, a guideline panel"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"Systematic review"}</b><span>{"about 13 weeks of work"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"The review this supports"}</b><span>{"Systematic review"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Reporting guideline"}</b><span>{"PRISMA 2020, with PRISMA-S for reporting the search strategy"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Registration"}</b><span>{"PROSPERO, before screening starts. Registering after screening has begun is visible in the record and is the point at which a reviewer stops taking the review at face value"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Databases, typically"}</b><span>{"5 — and the number is not what makes a review systematic"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Appraisal instrument"}</b><span><b style={{ color: "var(--ink)" }}>{"RoB 2 (Cochrane risk-of-bias tool for randomised trials)"}</b>{". Domain-based, judged per outcome rather than per study — which is why a single risk-of-bias rating for a whole trial is no longer acceptable."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Certainty of evidence"}</b><span>{"GRADE, reported per outcome rather than per review"}</span></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Why this one."}</b>{" A systematic review answers a defined question with a search anybody could repeat. The defining feature is not the number of databases; it is that the protocol existed before the search did, and that the decisions were made in advance rather than as the results came in."}</p><p><b>{"Your timeline."}</b> <span className={"tflag tflag--mid"}>{"Tight"}</span>{" Tight but workable. 12 weeks against roughly 13. It will hold if the search is run once and well rather than three times badly."}</p></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"One instrument we will not use, and why"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"The Jadad scale"}</b><span>{"Still cited by a great many medical writing sites. Cochrane advises against summary quality scores of this kind, because collapsing several unrelated domains into one number hides which domain was the problem — and a trial can score well while being at high risk of bias in the domain that matters for your outcome. Domain-based assessment replaced it, and RoB 2 judges risk per outcome rather than per study."}</span></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"How this was worked out."}</b>{" The review type follows from the question and the time, not from the label the author arrived with. Guidelines are as published: PRISMA 2020 and PRISMA-S at prisma-statement.org, PRISMA-ScR for scoping reviews, MOOSE for observational meta-analyses. Appraisal instruments follow the studies being appraised rather than the review doing the appraising: RoB 2 for randomised trials, ROBINS-I for non-randomised studies of interventions, QUADAS-3 for diagnostic accuracy since February 2026, AMSTAR 2 for systematic reviews, CASP with GRADE-CERQual for qualitative evidence. Week estimates are our own working figures at the scale each type usually runs to, and they assume the search is run once by somebody who builds searches for a living. "}<b>{"A regulatory literature review is a different product from a systematic review"}</b>{" and is judged against the submission template rather than against PRISMA."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"What makes a review systematic, and what does not"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"It is not the number of databases, and it is not the flow diagram. It is that the protocol existed before the search did. Everything a systematic review claims — that the question was fixed, that the inclusion criteria were not adjusted once the results were visible, that the outcomes reported are the ones planned — rests on the protocol predating the evidence. That is why PROSPERO registration matters and why the registration date is visible to anybody who looks: a review registered after screening began is not making a smaller claim, it is making the same claim without the thing that supported it. The second component is independent dual screening, because single screening misses studies at a rate that is well documented and not small. Everything else — six databases rather than four, grey literature, hand-searching reference lists — is a strength to be described honestly, not a qualifying condition. A three-database review with a registered protocol and dual screening is a systematic review. A nine-database review with neither is a literature search with a flow diagram on it."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-our-experts-klbwt1"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-sample-work-94a80x"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The three things a reviewer checks first."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not the conclusion. The search strategy, the flow of records, and the summary-of-findings table — because those three are where a review can be verified rather than believed. Use the tabs, then open the full sample below to read the complete search appendix and evidence summary on this page."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Systematic review · search appendix and evidence summary"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"An effect question · 5 databases · 3,914 records · 11 studies"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"The protocol · the search · the flow · the summary of findings"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the review"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cl-t1"} aria-controls={"cl-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Protocol"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cl-t2"} aria-controls={"cl-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"The search"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cl-t3"} aria-controls={"cl-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"The flow"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cl-t4"} aria-controls={"cl-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Certainty"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cl-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cl-t1"}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Registered"}</dt><dd>{"PROSPERO, eleven days before the first search was run. The date is permanent and visible, which is the entire point of it."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Population"}</dt><dd>{"Defined by diagnosis and care setting, with the age band stated rather than left as “adults”."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Intervention and comparator"}</dt><dd>{"Both specified, including what counts as usual care — which varies by country and is the commonest source of unexplained heterogeneity in this kind of review."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Outcomes, in a hierarchy"}</dt><dd>{"One primary, four secondary, ranked before the search. Ranking afterwards is outcome switching, it is checkable against the registration, and it is checked."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Appraisal instrument, named in advance"}</dt><dd>{"RoB 2, judged per outcome. Naming it afterwards invites the suspicion that it was chosen to suit the findings."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Analysis plan"}</dt><dd>{"Random-effects model stated in advance with the justification, plus the pre-specified subgroups and the sensitivity analyses. Three subgroups, not eleven."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Deviations"}</dt><dd>{"Two, both reported with their reasons in the final paper. Deviating is normal; deviating silently is not."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cl-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cl-t2"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"1"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"MEDLINE via Ovid · 1,182 records"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"MeSH terms exploded where appropriate, with free-text synonyms in title and abstract, truncation and adjacency operators in Ovid syntax. Strategy reproduced line by line in the appendix with its result counts."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"2"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Embase via Elsevier · 1,507 records"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Emtree rather than MeSH, because they are different vocabularies. Pasting a MEDLINE strategy into Embase is the single most common search error we see, and it silently loses studies rather than failing visibly."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"3"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Cochrane CENTRAL · 604 records"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Where the trials are. A review of randomised evidence that omits CENTRAL will be asked why."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"4"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Scopus and Web of Science · 621 records"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"For coverage outside the biomedical databases and for citation chasing forward from the key papers."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"5"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Trial registries and grey literature"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"ClinicalTrials.gov and the WHO ICTRP for completed-but-unpublished trials, which is where publication bias actually lives rather than in a funnel plot."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Tested against 4 known studies before running"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"All four retrieved. A strategy that misses papers you already know belong in the review is broken, and this test takes ten minutes against four thousand records of screening."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Every strategy saved with its date and interface"}</span><span>{"Re-runnable by a stranger"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cl-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cl-t3"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Records identified"}</dt><dd>{"3,914 from databases, 47 from registries and reference lists."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Duplicates removed"}</dt><dd>{"1,038. Reported as a number, because the deduplication rate tells a reader how much database overlap the search had."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Screened on title and abstract"}</dt><dd>{"2,923 by two reviewers independently. Agreement measured and reported."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Full texts sought"}</dt><dd>{"146. Four could not be obtained and are listed, because “not retrievable” is a reported category and leaving it out inflates the assessed set."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Full texts excluded"}</dt><dd>{"131, each with its reason: wrong comparator 58, wrong population 34, no extractable outcome 21, duplicate report of an included trial 12, not a trial 6. Reviewers read this list."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Studies included"}</dt><dd>{"11 studies in 15 reports. The distinction matters: a trial published as a primary paper and two secondary analyses is one study, and counting it as three is a real and common error."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"In the meta-analysis"}</dt><dd>{"9 of the 11 for the primary outcome. The two excluded are named with the reason, rather than disappearing between the flow diagram and the forest plot."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cl-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cl-t4"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"▣"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Primary outcome — moderate certainty"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Downgraded once for risk of bias: four of the nine trials were at high risk in the outcome-measurement domain because assessors were not blinded to allocation, and the outcome is subjective. Not downgraded for inconsistency, imprecision or indirectness."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"▣"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Secondary outcome one — low certainty"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Downgraded twice: once for imprecision, because the confidence interval spans both a clinically important benefit and a clinically important harm, and once for inconsistency that subgroup analysis did not explain."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"▣"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Secondary outcome two — very low certainty"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Reported by three of eleven studies. Selective outcome reporting is the likeliest explanation, and saying so is more useful to a reader than a pooled estimate from three trials."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Harms — not poolable"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Reported in four different ways across the eleven studies. Described narratively with each definition given, rather than forced into a common metric that none of the papers used."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"One certainty rating per outcome"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Not one for the review. A single overall GRADE rating is a misreading of the instrument and a reliable tell that the table was assembled at the end."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Every downgrade justified in a sentence"}</span><span>{"Checkable against the studies"}</span></p> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · topic and author details changed"}</span><span>{"Appendix and summary table, as delivered"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"A review is checked in three places, and the conclusion is not one of them. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The search tab is where reviews quietly fail."}</b>{" A MEDLINE strategy pasted into Embase looks like it worked — it returns records, the count is plausible, nothing errors. It is simply retrieving the wrong set, because MeSH and Emtree are different vocabularies. Testing the strategy against four studies you already know belong in the review costs ten minutes and catches it."}</p> <p><b>{"The flow tab has the distinction most authors miss."}</b>{" Eleven studies reported in fifteen papers is eleven studies. Counting the secondary analyses separately inflates the evidence base and is one of the errors a systematic review methodologist looks for first."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Protocol registered before screening"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"The date is permanent, and that is the point."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Search reported line by line, per database"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With dates, interfaces and counts, so it can be re-run."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Every full-text exclusion given a reason"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"A reported item, and one reviewers actually read."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Certainty graded per outcome"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With each downgrade justified in a checkable sentence."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a search appendix and evidence summary built round a question like yours — same field, same study types, same submission or journal."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-cl"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cl"}>{"Read the full appendix"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-cl"}> <span><b>{"Read the full search appendix and evidence summary"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the protocol, every search strategy, the flow, the appraisal, the synthesis and the GRADE table"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-cl"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Clinical literature review · sample appendix"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Search appendix, study flow and evidence summary"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A real review appendix with the clinical topic, the population and the author details changed, and the record counts adjusted so the review cannot be identified. The structure, the errors caught and the reporting are as delivered. Ask us and we will send one built around a question like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"Protocol and registration"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"As registered"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Registry and date"}</td><td>{"PROSPERO, registered 11 days before the first search was executed. Registration number quoted in the manuscript and in the appendix."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Population"}</td><td>{"Adults aged 18 and over with the index diagnosis, in secondary or tertiary care. Primary-care populations excluded and the exclusion justified, because the comparator differs materially."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Intervention"}</td><td>{"Defined by mechanism and dose range rather than by trade name, so that the search would retrieve trials using any of the agents in the class."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Comparator"}</td><td>{"Usual care, with what counts as usual care in each health system specified. This is the commonest unexamined source of heterogeneity in reviews of this kind."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Primary outcome"}</td><td>{"One, with its measurement instrument and time point named. Not “improvement”."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Secondary outcomes"}</td><td>{"Four, ranked. Ranking after the results are visible is outcome switching and is checkable against this record."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Risk of bias"}</td><td>{"RoB 2, judged per outcome, named in the protocol rather than chosen later."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Synthesis"}</td><td>{"Random-effects meta-analysis where two or more studies report a common outcome on a common metric; narrative synthesis otherwise. Three pre-specified subgroups. Two sensitivity analyses."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Protocol deviations"}</td><td>{"Two, both reported in the final paper with reasons: one subgroup dropped for lack of data, and one additional sensitivity analysis added at a reviewer’s request."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"Search strategies, as run"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Source"}</th><th>{"Interface and date"}</th><th>{"Records"}</th><th>{"Note"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"MEDLINE"}</td><td>{"Ovid, run once, date recorded"}</td><td>{"1,182"}</td><td>{"MeSH exploded where the tree supports it, with free-text synonyms in title, abstract and keyword fields. Adjacency operators rather than AND for the multi-word concepts."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Embase"}</td><td>{"Elsevier, same date"}</td><td>{"1,507"}</td><td>{"Rebuilt in Emtree, not translated from the MEDLINE strategy. Different vocabulary, different syntax, different results."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Cochrane CENTRAL"}</td><td>{"Wiley, same date"}</td><td>{"604"}</td><td>{"The primary source for randomised evidence, including trials indexed nowhere else."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Scopus"}</td><td>{"Elsevier, same date"}</td><td>{"391"}</td><td>{"Title-abstract-keyword search plus forward citation chasing from the four known studies."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Web of Science Core Collection"}</td><td>{"Clarivate, same date"}</td><td>{"230"}</td><td>{"For conference proceedings indexed there and not elsewhere."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"ClinicalTrials.gov and WHO ICTRP"}</td><td>{"Same date"}</td><td>{"39"}</td><td>{"Completed trials with no publication. This is where publication bias is actually found; a funnel plot with nine studies detects very little."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reference lists and citation chasing"}</td><td>{"Throughout"}</td><td>{"8"}</td><td>{"Backward from every included study and from three existing reviews."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Each strategy is reproduced in the appendix line by line with the result count at each line, which is what makes it re-runnable rather than merely described. Before execution, the MEDLINE strategy was tested against four studies known to belong in the review; all four were retrieved. This test costs ten minutes and is the only cheap way to find out that a strategy is quietly wrong."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"Study flow"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Stage"}</th><th>{"n"}</th><th>{"Detail"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Records identified, databases"}</td><td>{"3,914"}</td><td>{"Sum of the five databases above."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Records identified, other sources"}</td><td>{"47"}</td><td>{"Registries, reference lists, citation chasing."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Duplicates removed"}</td><td>{"1,038"}</td><td>{"Reported, because the rate tells a reader how much the databases overlapped."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Screened, title and abstract"}</td><td>{"2,923"}</td><td>{"Two reviewers, independently. Disagreements resolved by discussion; a third reader was needed for 14 records."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Excluded at screening"}</td><td>{"2,777"}</td><td>{"—"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Full texts sought"}</td><td>{"146"}</td><td>{"Four could not be obtained after contacting authors and interlibrary loan; all four are listed by citation."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Full texts assessed"}</td><td>{"142"}</td><td>{"Two reviewers, independently."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Excluded at full text"}</td><td>{"131"}</td><td>{"Wrong comparator 58; wrong population 34; no extractable outcome 21; duplicate report of an included trial 12; not a randomised trial 6. Every exclusion has a reason, and the list is published."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Studies included"}</td><td>{"11"}</td><td>{"Reported across 15 papers. Eleven studies, not fifteen — a primary report with two secondary analyses is one study."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"In the primary meta-analysis"}</td><td>{"9"}</td><td>{"Two included studies did not report the primary outcome on a combinable metric. Both are named, with the reason, rather than disappearing between the flow diagram and the forest plot."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Risk of bias, by domain and by outcome"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"RoB 2 domain"}</th><th>{"Low"}</th><th>{"Some concerns"}</th><th>{"High"}</th><th>{"What drove the judgements"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Randomisation process"}</td><td>{"8"}</td><td>{"3"}</td><td>{"0"}</td><td>{"Three trials described the sequence but not the concealment, which is “some concerns” rather than “high”."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Deviations from intended interventions"}</td><td>{"7"}</td><td>{"4"}</td><td>{"0"}</td><td>{"Four trials did not state whether the analysis was by intention to treat."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Missing outcome data"}</td><td>{"9"}</td><td>{"1"}</td><td>{"1"}</td><td>{"One trial lost 28% to follow-up with no analysis of whether loss differed by arm."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Measurement of the outcome"}</td><td>{"5"}</td><td>{"2"}</td><td>{"4"}</td><td>{"The primary outcome is subjective and four trials did not blind outcome assessors. This domain is why the primary outcome was downgraded."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Selection of the reported result"}</td><td>{"6"}</td><td>{"5"}</td><td>{"0"}</td><td>{"Five trials had no accessible protocol or registration to check the reported outcomes against."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Judged per outcome, not per study. The same trial can be at low risk for a mortality outcome and high risk for a subjective one, which is precisely why a single summary score per trial — the approach the Jadad scale takes — is no longer used. Cochrane advises against summary quality scores because they hide which domain was the problem."}</p> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"Summary of findings, with GRADE"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Outcome"}</th><th>{"Studies / participants"}</th><th>{"Certainty"}</th><th>{"Reason for the rating"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Primary outcome, at the pre-specified time point"}</td><td>{"9 studies / 2,104"}</td><td>{"Moderate"}</td><td>{"Downgraded once for risk of bias: four trials at high risk in outcome measurement, with a subjective outcome. No downgrade for inconsistency, indirectness or imprecision."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Secondary outcome 1"}</td><td>{"7 studies / 1,586"}</td><td>{"Low"}</td><td>{"Downgraded twice. Imprecision: the interval spans both an important benefit and an important harm. Inconsistency: unexplained by the pre-specified subgroups."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Secondary outcome 2"}</td><td>{"3 studies / 604"}</td><td>{"Very low"}</td><td>{"Reported by three of eleven studies. Selective reporting is the likeliest explanation, and saying so serves a reader better than a pooled estimate from three trials."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Secondary outcome 3"}</td><td>{"8 studies / 1,890"}</td><td>{"Moderate"}</td><td>{"Downgraded once for imprecision only."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Harms"}</td><td>{"11 studies / 2,431"}</td><td>{"Not pooled"}</td><td>{"Reported in four incompatible ways. Described narratively with each study’s definition given, rather than forced into a common metric none of them used."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"One certainty rating per outcome, each with its reason in a sentence a reader can check against the studies. A single overall rating for the review is a misreading of GRADE and a reliable sign that the table was assembled after the conclusion."}</p> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"What the review concluded, and what it did not"}</h4> <p>{"The pooled estimate for the primary outcome favoured the intervention, at moderate certainty. That is the finding. What the review explicitly did not conclude was that the intervention should be adopted: moderate certainty from nine trials with a subjective primary outcome and unblinded assessment in four of them supports a recommendation that is conditional rather than strong, and the discussion says so."}</p> <p>{"Two secondary outcomes were too uncertain to inform practice, and the review says that rather than reporting them alongside the primary as though they carried the same weight. Harms could not be pooled and are described. Publication bias could not be meaningfully assessed with nine studies, which is stated rather than tested and passed over — a funnel plot with nine points is decoration."}</p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"A review that reports its own limits is not a weaker review. It is the one a guideline panel can use, because the panel needs to know how far the evidence stretches before it decides what to recommend."}</p> <div className={"fsm__foot"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-clinical-literature-review-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What a Pubrica review delivers"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it gives you."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A review somebody else could repeat, with a conclusion proportionate to what the evidence actually carries."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The right review, chosen before the money is spent"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Systematic, rapid, scoping, umbrella, narrative or regulatory — decided from the question and the timeline rather than from the label in the proposal. The difference between two of these is a factor of three in cost and a completely different conclusion."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"A search a stranger could re-run"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Built by somebody who builds searches, rebuilt in each database’s own vocabulary rather than pasted between them, tested against studies you already know belong in the review, and reported line by line with dates, interfaces and counts."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Appraisal with the current instrument"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"RoB 2 per outcome, ROBINS-I with the version stated, QUADAS-3 rather than the superseded QUADAS-2, AMSTAR 2 for reviews. Domain judgements reported rather than a summary score, because a score hides which domain was the problem."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"A conclusion that will survive being checked"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Certainty graded per outcome with every downgrade justified, heterogeneity explained rather than reported, and the limits of the evidence stated plainly. An assessor who finds the gap you did not mention reads everything else differently."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-packages-1ej4o5c"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three tiers, with the scope printed beside the price."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Priced on the review type, the size of the field, the number of databases and whether the output is a journal paper or a submission. Every figure is a floor with its cap beside it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Starter"}</span> <h3>{"Narrative or targeted review"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Clinicians and early-career researchers who need the field summarised honestly, for a paper introduction, a grant background or a departmental decision"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $340"}</b><span>{"up to 30 sources · 2 databases · no registration"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"7–10 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The question framed, and the review type settled in writing first"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Search strategy documented per database, with dates and counts"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Thematic synthesis with the gaps named rather than asserted"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reference list in your target journal’s style, and the library delivered"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Labelled as narrative, honestly — no flow diagram on a non-systematic review"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: protocol and registration; dual screening; appraisal."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-cl"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cl"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Starter"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"Systematic review"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Researchers, guideline developers and clinical teams who need a review that will survive peer review on its method"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $760"}</b><span>{"up to 40 studies · 4–5 databases · registered protocol"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15–20 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Protocol to PRISMA-P, registered on PROSPERO before screening starts"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Search built per database and reported in full to PRISMA-S"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Independent dual screening at title, abstract and full text"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Risk of bias with the instrument that fits the studies, judged per outcome"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Narrative synthesis, GRADE per outcome and a summary-of-findings table"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"PRISMA 2020 flow diagram and the completed checklist with page numbers"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The extraction file and the reference library handed over, not just the report"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: meta-analysis; journal formatting and submission."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-cl"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cl"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Advanced"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Elite"}</span> <h3>{"With meta-analysis, or written into a submission"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Review authors pooling results, and regulatory, HTA and market access teams whose search will be audited"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,290"}</b><span>{"up to 60 studies · 5+ databases · grey literature and registries"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"20–30 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Advanced"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Meta-analysis with heterogeneity explored, not merely reported"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Pre-specified subgroups, meta-regression where the data supports it, sensitivity analyses that test the conclusion"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Forest and funnel plots built to journal specification, with the code returned"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Or: written into an MDR clinical evaluation, an HTA dossier or a regulatory submission, version-controlled and re-runnable to a stated date"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Journal formatting, submission and one round of response to reviewers"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Living reviews, network meta-analysis and annual search refreshes are quoted separately."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-cl"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cl"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Elite"}</a> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Additions are quoted alongside any tier: a living review with scheduled search refreshes; network meta-analysis; an annual search update for a clinical evaluation under the MDR, which is a recurring obligation rather than a one-off; screening support where your team has run out of capacity mid-review; translation and appraisal of non-English studies, which are excluded far more often for language than for relevance; a conference abstract or slide deck built from the review; and reference library migration between EndNote, Zotero and Mendeley. Article processing charges are paid by you directly to the journal and never passed through us."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-guarantee-15wg7th"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A review is only worth what its method can defend. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the review meets the brief and the guideline it is written to, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed and support running for a full year from delivery."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"365 days of revision support"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"On every tier. Journals take months, guideline panels meet quarterly, and a notified body may come back a year later. Support that expires in thirty days expires when you need it."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The search is re-runnable"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Every strategy delivered with its date, interface and counts. If somebody asks you to re-run it in eighteen months, you can, and so can they."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"You get the working files"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"The extraction sheet, the screening decisions, the reference library and any analysis code. Not just the report. The review belongs to you including its workings."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A database missed, a strategy mistranslated, a study wrongly excluded — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We cannot make thin evidence conclusive, and we will not write a synthesis that reads as more certain than the studies support — an HTA assessor or a notified body reviewer will find the same studies in an afternoon, and an optimistic characterisation tells them about the submitter rather than about the evidence. We will not call a review systematic if it was not: single-reviewer screening, an unregistered protocol or a search run after the inclusion criteria were adjusted all produce perfectly legitimate reviews, under their correct names. We will not remove a study from a synthesis because it is inconvenient, and we will not adjust inclusion criteria once the results are visible. We will not register a protocol retrospectively and present it as prospective, because the date is permanent and visible. And we cannot guarantee acceptance, because the decision belongs to an editor or an assessor."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The scoping answer is free"}</p> <p>{"Which review your question supports, how many weeks it is at that scale, and whether the literature can answer what you are asking. Two business days, no cost, no obligation. It is regularly the conversation that stops somebody commissioning a systematic review for a question that needed a scoping review, which is a difference of several thousand dollars and a different conclusion."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Authorship settled at the start"}</p> <p>{"Reviews have more contributors than papers and more disputes to match, because screening and extraction are visible, laborious and easy to undervalue. The author list is written down at the first meeting against the four ICMJE criteria, and a Pubrica contributor is acknowledged rather than authored unless the contribution genuinely meets all four — in which case we say so and you decide."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Confidentiality and data handling"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves. Unpublished protocols, commercial pipeline information and submission drafts are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, kept only as long as the project needs them, never used to train anything and never shared outside your project team. For regulatory work, documents are version-controlled so the file has a history rather than a final copy."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Instruments kept current"}</p> <p>{"Appraisal instruments and reporting guidelines are revised, and a review submitted against a superseded one gets asked about it. We check versions at the start of every project rather than carrying a list from the last one: QUADAS-3 replaced QUADAS-2 in February 2026; ROBINS-I V2 is circulating as a draft and is not yet settled, so we state which version we used; CONSORT and SPIRIT were both revised in 2025; PRISMA remains at 2020. Where a version we have quoted turns out to be superseded, we tell you and say what replaced it rather than quietly changing the page."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-client-storie-g3ntw"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three reviews, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named client has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“We were three weeks into screening before they told us the question was a scoping review. Stopping cost us a fortnight and saved us four months.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"EVIDENCE"}<br />{"SYNTHESIS"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Scoping"}<br />{"Review"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Clinical academic · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Our Embase search had been a pasted copy of the MEDLINE one for two years. Nobody had noticed because it returned results.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"MEDICAL"}<br />{"DEVICE"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Clinical"}<br />{"Evaluation"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Regulatory affairs lead · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Submitted as"}</b><span>{"Clinical evaluation report"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The GRADE table was the only part the guideline panel read closely, and it was the part we had left until last.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CLINICAL"}<br />{"GUIDELINE"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Systematic"}<br />{"Review"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Guideline methodologist · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-literature-review-faq-1jfquw3"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Clinical literature review FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Nine questions people ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure whether your question supports a systematic review, or whether your search would survive an audit? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-0"}><span>{"What is the difference between a systematic review and a clinical literature review?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"“Clinical literature review” is an umbrella term; “systematic review” is a specific method with conditions attached. A systematic review answers a pre-defined question using a protocol written and registered before the search, a search reported in enough detail for somebody else to run it, screening by two people independently, formal risk-of-bias assessment and a certainty rating. A clinical literature review may be any of six things: systematic, rapid, scoping, umbrella, narrative or a targeted review written into a regulatory submission. Each is legitimate under its own name. The problem is only ever the mismatch — a narrative review given a flow diagram, a scoping review asked for an effect estimate, a single-reviewer review called systematic. What makes a review systematic is not the number of databases; it is that the protocol existed before the evidence did."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-1"}><span>{"How do I conduct a clinical literature review for evidence-based medicine?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"In this order, and the order is the method. Frame the question so it can be searched — PICO for effect questions, SPIDER for qualitative, PIRD for diagnostic accuracy. Decide which review type the question and your timeline support. Write a protocol to PRISMA-P and register it on PROSPERO before you screen anything. Build the search in each database’s own vocabulary and test it against studies you already know belong in the review. Screen with two people independently, recording every full-text exclusion with its reason. Extract into a form you piloted first, with outcome data in duplicate. Appraise with the instrument that fits the studies. Then synthesise — narratively or by meta-analysis, decided from what the studies support — and grade certainty per outcome. Running these out of order is what quietly destroys the claim: adjusting inclusion criteria once the results are visible produces a perfectly readable review that no longer supports the thing it says about itself."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-2"}><span>{"Do I have to register the protocol?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"For a systematic review, yes in practice, and before screening begins rather than before submission. Registration is what supports every claim the review makes about its own method: that the question was fixed, that the inclusion criteria were not adjusted as the results appeared, that the outcomes reported are the ones planned and in the order planned. The registration date is permanently visible in PROSPERO, so a review registered after screening started is not making a smaller claim — it is making the same claim with the support removed, and reviewers check. Practical notes: PROSPERO takes systematic, rapid and umbrella reviews but not scoping reviews, which go to the Open Science Framework instead. Deviating from a registered protocol is entirely normal and happens in most reviews; what matters is reporting each deviation with its reason rather than quietly updating the record."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-3"}><span>{"Which tools should I use to appraise the studies?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"The instrument follows the studies being appraised, not the review doing the appraising. Randomised trials: RoB 2, judged per outcome rather than per study, because the same trial can be at low risk for mortality and high risk for a subjective outcome. Non-randomised studies of interventions: ROBINS-I, and state which version, because ROBINS-I V2 has circulated as a draft and is not yet settled. Exposure studies: ROBINS-E. Diagnostic accuracy: QUADAS-3, which superseded QUADAS-2 in February 2026 — a review submitted now using QUADAS-2 will be asked about it. Systematic reviews, in an umbrella review: AMSTAR 2. Qualitative research: a CASP checklist, with GRADE-CERQual for confidence in the findings. What we do not use is the Jadad scale, which is still listed on a great many review pages. Cochrane advises against summary quality scores, because collapsing several domains into one number hides which domain was the problem, and domain-based assessment replaced them more than a decade ago."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-4"}><span>{"How many databases do I need?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Fewer than people think, and chosen rather than counted. For a review of randomised evidence in a biomedical field, MEDLINE, Embase and the Cochrane Library cover most of it, with trial registries for completed-but-unpublished trials. Scopus or Web of Science add coverage outside the biomedical core and let you chase citations forward. CINAHL matters for nursing and allied health, PsycINFO for mental health, and regional databases — LILACS, African Journals Online, CNKI — matter far more than most English-language reviews acknowledge. What does not improve a review is adding a sixth database to the list and running the same badly translated strategy in it. Two well-built searches retrieve more than five pasted ones, because the vocabularies genuinely differ: MeSH in MEDLINE and Emtree in Embase are different thesauri, and a MEDLINE strategy pasted into Embase returns plausible-looking results from the wrong set. Report what you searched and, just as importantly, what you did not and why."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-5"}><span>{"Can one person do a systematic review?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"One person can do an excellent review, but not one that meets the usual conditions for calling it systematic, because independent dual screening is one of them. Single-reviewer screening misses eligible studies at a rate that is well documented and not small, and the misses are not random — they cluster in the records that are ambiguous from the abstract, which are disproportionately the interesting ones. There are two honest routes. Do it as a rapid review and say in the methods exactly which systematic-review steps were abbreviated and why, which is a respected and widely published form. Or bring in a second screener for the screening stage only, which is the cheapest part of the review to buy and the one where a second pair of eyes changes the result. What does not work is single screening described in a way that leaves a reader to assume otherwise."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-6"}><span>{"What if the search returns almost nothing?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"First check that it is the field and not the strategy, which is why testing against known studies before running matters. If the search is sound and the field really is thin, that is a finding rather than a failure, and it is often a more useful one than the review you were expecting. A well-documented empty or near-empty review tells a guideline panel that no recommendation can be made, tells a funder exactly where the gap is, and tells a trialist what the next study should be. Empty reviews are published and are cited. What does not work is widening the inclusion criteria until something appears, because the criteria were registered, the change is visible, and a review whose scope expanded after the results were seen cannot claim what a systematic review claims. Where we find this we will say so and set out the honest options: report the gap, reframe the question deliberately and re-register, or stop."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-7"}><span>{"Is a regulatory literature review the same as a systematic review?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and treating them as the same is expensive in both directions. A literature review inside an EU MDR clinical evaluation, an IVDR performance evaluation, an HTA submission or a regulatory dossier is a controlled document within a technical file. It is judged by an auditor or an assessor against the submission’s own template and expectations, it carries a version history rather than a publication date, and it has to be re-runnable to a stated date because the obligation recurs — a clinical evaluation is updated, not finished. It also frequently has to appraise evidence about a specific device or product rather than answer a general effect question, which changes the search entirely. A systematic review written to PRISMA is not wrong in this setting, and PRISMA is genuinely the clearest available structure for reporting the search, but it answers a different question and takes roughly twice as long. Conversely, a regulatory literature review submitted to a journal will be asked why there is no protocol registration."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cl-8"}><span>{"How long does a systematic review actually take?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cl-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Published estimates for academic teams run to a year or more, though much of that is elapsed time rather than work — people screening in the evenings between other commitments. As concentrated work at the scale most clinical reviews run to, budget something like three weeks of reviewer time across all stages, with screening the largest single block and full-text retrieval the step that always takes longer than anyone plans for. The variables that actually move the number are the size of the search, whether screening is dual, how many studies survive to extraction, and whether authors have to be contacted for missing data. The chooser at the top of this page gives an estimate for your parameters, and our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/free-tools/"} data-nav={""}>{"free screening workload estimator"}</a>{" breaks the same figure down stage by stage with every rate as an editable field, so you can argue with ours. The most reliable way to make a review take too long is a search that returns four thousand records to find forty studies — an hour with somebody who builds searches saves more time than any amount of screening speed."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of a review."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A review needs a search behind it and a home in front of it, and both are work in their own right."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"BEFORE THE REVIEW"}</b><em>{"the question and the search"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/literature-search-and-citation"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature search and citation"}</b><span>{"The search itself, built per database and reported so it can be re-run."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature review and gap analysis"}</b><span>{"The gap demonstrated so a reviewer can check it, rather than asserted."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"IF IT POOLS"}</b><em>{"the numbers"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/meta-analysis/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Meta-analysis"}</b><span>{"Heterogeneity explored and explained, not reported and passed over."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/systematic-review/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Systematic review writing"}</b><span>{"The full method, from protocol registration to the summary of findings."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"WHERE IT ENDS UP"}</b><em>{"a journal, or a submission"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Physician manuscripts"}</b><span>{"The review written up as a paper, to the guideline its type requires."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical and regulatory writing"}</b><span>{"The clinical evaluation report the literature review sits inside."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on evidence synthesis."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on structure, journal choice and writing for readers outside the specialty."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the question. We will tell you which review it supports."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Which review type, how many weeks of work at that scale, and an honest read on whether the literature can answer what you are asking — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
